Failure handling and synchronization
ReadBarTicks() returns the tick count, or -1 on failure. On failure it records
GetLastError()
and clears the output array, so no partial data is ever used. The caller can then mark the bar incomplete instead of plotting a false zero.
Tick history is synchronized on demand. The first request for a symbol or period may fail, or return nothing, while the terminal downloads ticks from the server. A return of 0 is therefore ambiguous, because it can mean a quiet bar or a missing download. The indicator uses the bar tick volume as a hint, and the hint has limits, as described later.
