Classifying Ticks with the Tick Rule: TickClassifier.mqh
This class turns a single price change into a direction. It holds no state and calls no terminal functions, so the caller supplies everything the rule needs. That choice makes the tick rule the easiest part of the project to test, and the most important one to get exactly right.
The class has three methods. ClassifyDirection() applies the rule, ExtractPrice() reads the chosen price from a tick, and ExtractVolume() reads the chosen volume. The first listing shows the class declaration with its constructor and destructor.
