Aggregating the ticks of one bar
AggregateTicks() walks the tick array in time order. The state parameter is both input and output. It is the starting state, and it advances tick by tick. That is how state crosses bar boundaries, because the caller passes the stored state of the previous bar into the next one.
Each tick lands in exactly one bucket, and ticks with an invalid price are skipped and not counted. So tick_count is the number of valid ticks, not the number CopyTicksRange() returned. The totals are derived once at the end, so the identities hold by construction. Total volume equals buy plus sell plus unclassified volume, and delta equals buy minus sell volume. The delta ratio is guarded against a zero total.
//+------------------------------------------------------------------+
//| AggregateTicks                                                   |
//+------------------------------------------------------------------+
void
CTickDeltaAggregator::AggregateTicks(
const
MqlTick
&ticks[],
const
datetime
bar_time,
const
ENUM_OF_PRICE_SOURCE source,
const
ENUM_OF_VOLUME_MODE mode,
      CTickState &state,
      CBarDelta &result)
  {
   result.Reset();
   result.bar_time=bar_time;
   result.data_complete=
true
;
//--- walk every tick in chronological order
int
total=::
ArraySize
(ticks);
for
(
int
i=
0
; i<total; i++)
     {
double
price=
0.0
;
if
(!m_classifier.ExtractPrice(ticks[i],source,price))
continue
;
double
volume=
0.0
;
if
(!m_classifier.ExtractVolume(ticks[i],mode,volume))
         volume=
0.0
;
