Cumulative series and the daily reset
BuildCumulativeSeries() converts per-bar deltas into a running total. All arrays are chronological, with index 0 as the oldest bar. The start parameter lets the caller recompute only a tail, because the running total at start minus one is the seed.
An undefined bar is flagged undefined, and the running total passes through it unchanged. Later totals are therefore offset by the missing delta, so treat cumulative values after a data hole with caution. The method returns false when the arrays are too small, and the indicator checks that result.
With the daily reset on, the total returns to zero on the first bar whose server-time day differs from the previous bar. This is a calendar day on the server clock, not an exchange trading session. Weekends, breaks, and session schedules are not modeled. The running total starts at zero at the first bar of the last full calculation, so the first day is a partial total. That base does not move as new bars arrive.
IsDifferentDay() compares whole days since the epoch. ColorIndexForDelta() gives an exact zero, or an undefined delta, the neutral index, so zero is never colored green or red.
